<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramón Grau San Martín</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1881">1881</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramón Grau San Martín was a Cuban physician and politician who headed the revolutionary 'Hundred Days' government of 1933–1934, which decreed labour and social reforms before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulgencio-batista">Fulgencio Batista</a> forced him out. He founded the Auténtico Party and was elected president in 1944, serving until 1948, but his government became known for corruption and gang violence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramon-grau-san-martin.jpg" alt="Ramón Grau San Martín" width="301" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: official picture · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ram%C3%B3n_Grau_San_Mart%C3%ADn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
